  name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-8222186-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>8222186</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </patcit><patcit ucid="JP-8329732-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>8329732</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id> <sources><source name="APP" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </patcit> <patcit ucid="JP-9027213-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9027213</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1186829A1</text><sources><source name="APP" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HAMAMATSU PHOTONICS KK</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ITO MASAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SEI YUJIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HAMAMATSU PHOTONICS K.K.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ITO, MASAKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEI, YUJIRO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ITO MASAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SEI YUJIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ITO, MASAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEI, YUJIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A portable light source comprises a lamp (10) contained in a lamp box (42), which is housed in a case (41) to significantly reduce the influences of ambient temperature.  In other words, the deuterium lamp (10), likely to be influenced by temperature, is enclosed in a double shield structure including the case (41) as well as the lamp box (42).  As a result, the deuterium lamp (10) is kept fairly insensitive to the change in temperature of the case (41) that is most affected by ambient temperature, so the light source can be used outdoors regardless of the weather and indoors regardless of the influence of the air conditioner.  Since the lamp box (42) is adapted to receive the deuterium lamp (10) through its top, the lamp (10) can be easily replaced if the case (41) is designed compact, thus increasing the portability of the light source outdoors.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention se rapporte à une source de lumière portable comportant une lampe (10) contenue dans un logement de lampe (42), qui est enfermé dans un boîtier (41) conçu pour réduire considérablement l'influence de la température ambiante. En d'autres termes, la lampe au deutérium (10), qui est susceptible de subir l'influence de la température, est enfermée dans une double structure protectrice constituée du boîtier (41) et du logement de lampe (42). De ce fait, la lampe au deutérium (10) est sensiblement à l'abri des changements de température ambiante, de sorte que la source de lumière peut être utilisée en extérieur quelles que soient les conditions météorologiques et en intérieur quelle que soit l'influence de la climatisation. Etant donné que le logement de lampe (42) est conçu pour recevoir la lampe au deutérium (10) par sa partie supérieure, la lampe peut être facilement remplacée si le boîtier (41) est conçu de manière compacte, ce qui accroît la portabilité de cette source de lumière à l'extérieur.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>